### STAGE 5 — Skills, persona_access, draft-skill governance

```
knowledge/skills/business/*.md   (persona_access: [business, manager])
knowledge/skills/developer/*.md  (persona_access: [developer])
```
Build `skill_match.py` (filters by `persona_access`), `draft_skill_node.py` (per Part A), `app/admin/review_queue.py` (approve/reject endpoints).

**Exit condition**: business-role user matches only business skills; an unmatched question produces a `skill_gap_log` row + a pending `content_review_queue` item + a graceful fallback answer, with nothing auto-written to `knowledge/skills/`.

### STAGE 6 — Real model wiring (you have this now — do it today)

```python
import anthropic
client = anthropic.Anthropic(api_key=os.environ["ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"])
def call_model(prompt: str) -> str:
    r = client.messages.create(model="claude-sonnet-4-6", max_tokens=1024,
        messages=[{"role": "user", "content": prompt}])
    return r.content[0].text
```
Add prompt caching (static system prompt + persona instructions first, dynamic content last, per the caching design).

**Exit condition**: real, cited answers on all 5 test questions.

### STAGE 7 — Gates + evals

Wrap router output in one `run_gates()` function (Permission, Evidence, Freshness, Quality, Action, Memory). Build `app/evals/golden_questions.py` (15-20 real questions) + `eval_runner.py`.

**Exit condition**: eval suite runs, logs to `eval_case_log`, confidence scores vary meaningfully (not always 0 or 1).

### STAGE 8 — RBAC/leakage test suite (highest priority open item)

```python
