### STAGE 11 — CI/CD

```yaml
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml — both repos
test → security-scan → build-push (ECR) → deploy-dev → smoke-test → [manual approval] → stg → [manual approval] → prod
```
Weekly skill-review Action per the earlier design.

**Exit condition**: pipeline green end-to-end against a test push.

### STAGE 12 — Infra request (Terraform + Helm, already built)

Submit PR: namespace (`forge-dev`) + NetworkPolicy, IRSA (2 roles, scoped exactly), RDS+pgvector (not in-cluster), DNS (`forge-gateway-dev.k8s.internal.capitalgroup.com`, `forge-ui-dev...`), egress confirmation (github.com, graph.microsoft.com, Atlassian, bedrock endpoint), CI/CD OIDC access.

**Exit condition**: `terraform plan` reviewed and approved.

### STAGE 13 — Deploy DEV

```bash
flyway -url=jdbc:postgresql://<rds-endpoint>/forge migrate
helm upgrade --install forge-api-gateway ./infra/helm -f values-dev.yaml --set image.tag=$SHA -n forge-dev
curl https://forge-gateway-dev.k8s.internal.capitalgroup.com/health
# gateway alone, verified, THEN:
helm upgrade --install forge-ui ./infra/helm -f values-dev.yaml --set image.tag=$SHA -n forge-dev
```
**Exit condition**: full test suite green against the DEV URL, not just local.

### STAGE 14 — STG, then PROD

Second `team_id` onboarded in STG to prove multi-tenant isolation under real conditions. RDS Proxy, HPA, Karpenter, CloudFront, Redis cluster-mode added per the production-scale design. Bedrock quota increase requested once real STG traffic data exists.

**Exit condition**: RBAC/leakage + eval suites green in CI on every PR; Doug/stakeholder demo approved; PROD deploy with Multi-AZ, real secrets, full observability.

