## PART D — Go-live priority order (fastest safe path)

1. **Today**: Stage 6 (real Anthropic model, unblocked now) + Stage 8 (RBAC/leakage — highest priority)
2. **This week**: Stages 1-7, 9 completed and verified locally
3. **Next**: Stage 10 (frontend/BFF), Stage 11 (CI/CD)
4. **In parallel with the above**: Stage 12 (Terraform PR submission — doesn't block local work)
5. **Once infra lands**: Stage 13 (DEV deploy)
6. **After DEV is stable + Doug demo done**: Stage 14 (STG → PROD)

**The one rule that keeps this fast without becoming reckless**: never start a stage before the previous one's exit condition is met. Every debugging session in this entire build happened because a later layer was built on an unverified earlier one — skipping verification to "go faster" has already cost more time than it saved, every time it happened.
